window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-f780ae4c53905f80"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"bedrock-govcloud-configuration\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"govcloud-bedrock\">在 GovCloud 中配置 Bedrock</h1> <blockquote> <p>如需查看完整文档索引，请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取 Markdown 格式的文档。</p> </blockquote> <p>本指南说明如何配置 Codex，使其通过 Amazon Bedrock 在 GovCloud 中执行推理。内容涵盖 AWS 访问、受管设备设置和网络控制。</p> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-c2332644faa13713\">Codex 配置参考</a></p> <p>本指南不是法律意见，也不会授予你运营授权（authorization to operate，ATO）。请依据机构要求和系统安全计划，与安全及授权负责人一起审查配置、所选 AWS 服务、端点控制和数据流。</p> <p><a id=\"shared-responsibility\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_1\">共同责任</h2> <p>请查看 <a href=\"https://aws.amazon.com/compliance/shared-responsibility-model/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">AWS 共同责任模型（需联网）</a>以及你所选服务的文档，了解 AWS 提供哪些控制措施。你的机构负责批准使用这些服务。</p> <p>在受支持的部署中，Codex 会使用 AWS 身份验证，向已配置的 Bedrock 端点发送推理请求。你的组织需要保护运行 Codex 的设备，包括凭据、代码库、本地记录和已启用的第三方服务。仅在推理环节使用 GovCloud，并不能证明整个工作流程符合机构要求。</p> <p><strong>govcloud-setup</strong></p> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-f780ae4c53905f80?anchor=3-verify-the-deployment\">验证清单</a> · <a href=\"#/article/a-f780ae4c53905f80?anchor=feature-settings\">功能设置</a></p> <p><a id=\"before-you-begin\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">开始之前</h2> <p>请使用 <strong>26.1002.51308 或更高版本的桌面应用</strong>；可在 <strong>About</strong>（关于）中查看版本号。</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>准备事项</th> <th>所需内容</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>AWS 访问权限</td> <td>一个可访问你计划使用的 Bedrock 模型的 AWS GovCloud 账户。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>配置</td> <td>已审核的 <code>requirements.toml</code>、获批的网络目标，以及回滚说明。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>设备管理</td> <td>系统配置或 MDM 访问权限，并具备针对应用、设备和代理命令的网络策略。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"1-deploy-device-requirements\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"1\">1. 部署设备要求</h2> <p>在启动应用前，通过系统配置或 MDM 部署 <code>requirements.toml</code>。请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-77481efb12a63f4e\">受管配置</a>，了解文件位置和 MDM 下发方式。保护好受管策略，并在<a href=\"#/article/a-f780ae4c53905f80?anchor=3-verify-the-deployment\">第 3 步</a>中确认运行 Codex 的计算机已应用相关设置。</p> <p><a id=\"recommended-requirementstoml\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"requirementstoml\">推荐的 <code>requirements.toml</code></h3> <p>下方默认 <code>requirements.toml</code> 有意采用严格限制。管理员可以启用其他功能，但需要接受这些功能带来的风险。请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-f780ae4c53905f80?anchor=feature-settings\">功能文档</a>和<a href=\"#/article/a-77481efb12a63f4e?anchor=configure-network-access-requirements\">网络控制文档</a>。</p> <p>requirements.toml</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\"># Disable ChatGPT sign-in.\nallowed_login_methods = [\"api\"]\n\n# https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/agent-approvals-security#common-sandbox-and-approval-combinations\nallowed_sandbox_modes = [\"read-only\", \"workspace-write\"]\n\n# Approval prompts are reviewed by the user.\nallowed_approvals_reviewers = [\"user\"]\nallowed_approval_policies = [\n  { granular = { sandbox_approval = false, rules = true, mcp_elicitations = false, request_permissions = false, skill_approval = true } },\n]\n\n# Allow cached search only if your AWS GovCloud Region supports web search.\nallowed_web_search_modes = [\"disabled\", \"cached\"]\n\n# Block agent browser use and native-app control.\nallow_browser_and_computer_use = false\n\n# Appshots: https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/appshots\nallow_appshots = false\n\n# Remote control: https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/remote-connections#pick-up-work-from-another-device\nallow_remote_control = false\n\n# Managed hooks: https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/enterprise/managed-configuration#enforce-managed-hooks-from-requirements\nallow_managed_hooks_only = true\n\ncheck_for_update_on_startup = false\n\n# MCP servers, apps, and plugins are disabled by default.\n# Admins can enable supported integrations after accepting the risks\n# for their use case and configuring access and network controls.\n# https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/enterprise/managed-configuration\nmcp_servers = {}\n\n[features]\napps = false\nenable_mcp_apps = false\nplugins = false\n\n# Enable the network proxy for sandboxed commands.\n# https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/agent-approvals-security#network-isolation\nnetwork_proxy = true\n\nin_app_dictation = false\nrealtime_conversation = false\n\n# Browser controls: https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/enterprise/managed-configuration#disable-codex-feature-surfaces\n# Note that both browser use and computer use are up to your organization's risk appetite.\n# An agent using your browser or computer may navigate to any websites or applications that the\n# computer has access to. OpenAI does not currently provide additional protections restricting\n# the network paths that browser use and computer use may exercise.\nin_app_browser = false\nbrowser_use = false\nbrowser_use_external = false\nbrowser_use_full_cdp_access = false\n\n# Computer Use: https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/computer-use\n# Enable after accepting the risks and configuring app and network access.\ncomputer_use = false\n\n# Set to true to let users update through the app.\n# App-store, package-manager, and MDM updates are controlled separately.\n# https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/enterprise/manage-app-updates#turn-off-in-app-updates\nin_app_updates = false\n\nimage_generation = false\n\n# Memories: https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/customization/memories\nmemories = false\n\n# Computer History: https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/customization/computer-history\nchronicle = false\n\nexternal_agent_memory_import = false\n\n# We recommend that users review approval requests themselves.\n# Admins can enable automatic review after accepting the risks for their use case.\n# https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/agent-approvals-security#automatic-approval-reviews\nguardian_approval = false\nguardianv2 = false\n\n# Disable background skill-search experiments.\nskill_search = false\n\n# Hooks: https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/hooks\nhooks = false\n\n# If you enable web search, use cached search through Bedrock Mantle\n# where supported by your AWS GovCloud Region.\nstandalone_web_search = false\n\n# Disable feedback submissions to OpenAI.\n[feedback]\nenabled = false\n\n# Network controls for agent commands:\n# https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/enterprise/managed-configuration#configure-network-access-requirements\n[experimental_network]\nenabled = true\nmanaged_allowed_domains_only = true\n\n# No domains allowed by default. Add destinations approved for your use case.\ndomains = {}\n\n# Add approved Unix socket paths here.\nunix_sockets = {}\n\n# Set to true when using an organization-approved upstream proxy.\nallow_upstream_proxy = false\n\n# Keep the command proxy bound to localhost.\ndangerously_allow_non_loopback_proxy = false\ndangerously_allow_all_unix_sockets = false\n\n# Local/private networking: https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/agent-approvals-security#local-and-private-destinations\nallow_local_binding = false\n\n# App network controls: https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/enterprise/managed-configuration#control-desktop-app-network-destinations\n[application.network]\nenabled = true\n\n# Example: Bedrock Mantle in us-gov-west-1.\n# Replace this hostname with the Bedrock endpoint configured in config.toml.\n[application.network.domains]\n\"bedrock-mantle.us-gov-west-1.api.aws\" = \"allow\"\n\n# OpenAI and ChatGPT endpoints.\n# We recommend denying these endpoints to avoid any risk that user data is sent to commercial OpenAI infrastructure.\n\"api.openai.com\" = \"deny\"\n\"chat.openai.com\" = \"deny\"\n\"chatgpt.com\" = \"deny\"\n\"ab.chatgpt.com\" = \"deny\"\n\"platform.openai.com\" = \"deny\"\n\"auth.openai.com\" = \"deny\"\n\"gov.api.openai.com\" = \"deny\"\n\"gov.chatgpt.com\" = \"deny\"\n\"sdfedpreastus2.oaiusercontent.com\" = \"deny\"\n\"o33249.ingest.us.sentry.io\" = \"deny\"\n\"persistent.oaistatic.com\" = \"deny\"\n\"oaisidekickupdates.blob.core.windows.net\" = \"deny\"\n\n# Windows only: https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/config-file/config-reference#requirementstoml\n[windows]\nallowed_sandbox_implementations = [\"elevated\"]\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"2-configure-provider-routing-and-network-controls\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"2\">2. 配置提供方路由与网络控制</h2> <p>在 <code>config.toml</code> 或受管默认值中设置 provider、model、Region（区域）和 endpoint（端点）。用户可以在 <code>requirements.toml</code> 设定的范围内更改这些默认值。</p> <p><a id=\"recommended-configtoml\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"configtoml\">推荐的 <code>config.toml</code></h3> <p>下方示例使用 <code>us-gov-west-1</code> 中的 Mantle。请将模型 ID 和 AWS profile 替换为你部署中的实际值。若要使用其他受支持的区域或端点，请同步更新 URL、区域和网络策略。</p> <p>示例关闭了可选诊断和数据共享。请勿将 AWS 凭据放入 TOML 文件。AWS profile、凭据和凭据助手脚本应放在 Codex 无权修改的文件夹之外。</p> <p>config.toml</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\"># Replace with your approved Bedrock model ID.\nmodel = \"openai.gpt-5.6-terra\"\nmodel_provider = \"amazon-bedrock\"\napproval_policy = { granular = { sandbox_approval = false, rules = true, mcp_elicitations = false, request_permissions = false, skill_approval = true } }\nsandbox_mode = \"workspace-write\"\n\n# Set to \"cached\" only when supported by your model and GovCloud Region\n# and approved for your deployment.\n# https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/web-search.html\nweb_search = \"disabled\"\n\n# Example: Bedrock Mantle in us-gov-west-1.\n[model_providers.amazon-bedrock]\nbase_url = \"https://bedrock-mantle.us-gov-west-1.api.aws/openai/v1\"\nwire_api = \"responses\"\nrequires_openai_auth = false\n\n[model_providers.amazon-bedrock.aws]\nregion = \"us-gov-west-1\"\n\n# Replace with your AWS profile name.\nprofile = \"codex-govcloud\"\n\n[sandbox_workspace_write]\n# Command destinations are controlled by requirements.toml.\nnetwork_access = true\n\n# Disable sending Codex usage analytics to OpenAI.\n[analytics]\nenabled = false\n\n# OpenTelemetry exports are off by default.\n# Admins can configure an approved collector for logs, traces, and metrics.\n# https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/config-file/config-advanced#observability-and-telemetry\n[otel]\nexporter = \"none\"\ntrace_exporter = \"none\"\nmetrics_exporter = \"none\"\nlog_user_prompt = false\n</code></pre> <p>本示例使用 AWS 凭据连接 Bedrock Mantle。若要使用 Bedrock Runtime 或网关，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-fc9fbba758a53038\">提供方设置说明</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"apply-network-controls\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_3\">应用网络控制</h3> <p>将 Bedrock 等获批的应用端点添加到 <a href=\"#/article/a-77481efb12a63f4e?anchor=control-desktop-app-network-destinations\"><code>application.network.domains</code></a>。将获批的命令端点添加到 <a href=\"#/article/a-77481efb12a63f4e?anchor=configure-network-access-requirements\"><code>experimental_network.domains</code></a>。</p> <p>Codex 的网络设置不能替代设备防火墙。</p> <h2 id=\"3-verify-the-deployment\">3. 验证部署</h2> <ol> <li>确认策略处于启用状态，并且 Codex 使用了预期的 AWS 凭据和 Bedrock 设置。</li> <li>使用示例数据运行获批的工作流程。</li> <li>确认用户设置无法覆盖受管限制。</li> <li>测试无效或过期凭据以及路由失败的情况，并确认内容不会被发送到未获批准的目标。</li> </ol> <p><a id=\"troubleshoot-common-problems\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">排查常见问题</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>问题</th> <th>检查事项</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>端点不受支持</td> <td>向 OpenAI 确认已安装的桌面应用和 app-server 版本支持该端点与模型。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>AWS 账户或角色不正确</td> <td>检查当前凭据和所选 AWS profile。Bedrock API key 可能优先于 profile 生效。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>限制未生效</td> <td>确认运行 Codex 的计算机加载了预期的 <code>requirements.toml</code>。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>功能仍不可用</td> <td>查看功能文档，确认所需设置及 Bedrock 支持情况，然后检查网络控制。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"feature-settings\">功能设置</h2> <p>用户无法覆盖由 <code>requirements.toml</code> 强制执行的功能设置。</p> <p>下表总结了上述配置。<strong>On（开启）</strong>表示在受支持的情况下允许使用；其他权限和网络控制仍然适用。</p> <p>有关提供方支持情况，请参阅 <a href=\"#/article/a-fc9fbba758a53038?anchor=feature-availability\">Bedrock 功能可用性</a>。</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>功能</th> <th>默认状态</th> <th>说明</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>本地编码、文件、Git 和子代理</td> <td>On</td> <td>—</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-b5406e60cbfa0b68\">本地计划任务</a></td> <td>On</td> <td>—</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-a7de5b39bd26a809\">浏览器</a></td> <td>Off</td> <td>包括内置浏览器、已连接的浏览器、代理浏览器控制和 Developer mode（开发者模式）。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-7be3f970bd43699c\">Computer Use（计算机使用）</a>和 <a href=\"#/article/a-c302b8efa03eab38\">Appshots</a></td> <td>Off</td> <td>—</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-7ea5a1f5cc6a25bc\">记忆</a>和<a href=\"#/article/a-f3a0216fc3d2956b\">计算机历史记录</a></td> <td>Off</td> <td>—</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-6e5b50840145f8df\">图像生成</a></td> <td>Off</td> <td>不会阻止输入图像或读取现有图像文件。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-eb946260804133fb\">网页搜索</a></td> <td>Off</td> <td>缓存搜索需要模型和 GovCloud 区域支持。命令网络规则不会限制托管式搜索。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">应用和插件</a></td> <td>Off</td> <td>—</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-77481efb12a63f4e\">已配置的 MCP 服务器</a></td> <td>Off</td> <td>管理员可以在接受相应使用风险并配置访问和网络控制后，启用获批服务器。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>交互式 MCP 应用</td> <td>Off</td> <td>—</td> </tr> <tr> <td>听写</td> <td>Off</td> <td>—</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-b7af4e0dbfe643b3?anchor=automatic-approval-reviews\">自动审批审查</a></td> <td>Off</td> <td>—</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-171fdaa74f75310f?anchor=pick-up-work-from-another-device\">远程控制</a></td> <td>Off</td> <td>SSH 连接是单独的功能。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-24c62848a3326493\">应用更新</a></td> <td>Off</td> <td>—</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>若要启用代理浏览器功能或 Computer Use，还必须设置 <code>allow_browser_and_computer_use = true</code>。</p> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-f780ae4c53905f80?anchor=3-verify-the-cli-deployment\">验证清单</a> · <a href=\"#/article/a-f780ae4c53905f80?anchor=cli-feature-settings\">功能设置</a></p> <p>配置 Codex CLI，使其通过 Amazon Bedrock 在 GovCloud 中执行推理。<a href=\"#/article/a-f780ae4c53905f80?anchor=shared-responsibility\">共同责任指南</a>同样适用于 CLI 部署。</p> <h2 id=\"cli-prerequisites\">开始之前</h2> <p>请安装 <a href=\"#/article/a-24d888be8e5fa72d\">Codex CLI</a>，并检查已安装的版本：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-shell\">codex --version\n</code></pre> <p>请使用 <strong>Codex CLI 0.162.0 或更高版本</strong>。</p> <p>你需要一个可访问计划使用的 Bedrock 模型的 AWS GovCloud 账户，并需要管理员权限，以便在运行 Codex 的计算机上部署 <code>requirements.toml</code>。若在 WSL 或 SSH 环境中使用 CLI，请在 CLI 实际运行的环境内应用配置。</p> <h2 id=\"1-deploy-cli-requirements\">1. 部署 CLI 要求</h2> <p>在启动 CLI 前，通过系统配置或 MDM 部署 <code>requirements.toml</code>。请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-77481efb12a63f4e\">受管配置</a>，了解文件位置和 MDM 下发方式。保护好受管策略，并在<a href=\"#/article/a-f780ae4c53905f80?anchor=3-verify-the-cli-deployment\">第 3 步</a>中确认运行 Codex 的计算机已应用相关设置。</p> <h3 id=\"cli-recommended-requirementstoml\"> 推荐的 <code>requirements.toml</code> </h3> <p>下方默认 <code>requirements.toml</code> 有意采用严格限制。管理员可以启用其他功能，但需要接受这些功能带来的风险。请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-f780ae4c53905f80?anchor=cli-feature-settings\">功能文档</a>和<a href=\"#/article/a-77481efb12a63f4e?anchor=configure-network-access-requirements\">网络控制文档</a>。</p> <p>requirements.toml</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\"># Disable ChatGPT sign-in.\nallowed_login_methods = [\"api\"]\n\n# https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/agent-approvals-security#common-sandbox-and-approval-combinations\nallowed_sandbox_modes = [\"read-only\", \"workspace-write\"]\n\n# Approval prompts are reviewed by the user.\nallowed_approvals_reviewers = [\"user\"]\nallowed_approval_policies = [\n  { granular = { sandbox_approval = false, rules = true, mcp_elicitations = false, request_permissions = false, skill_approval = true } },\n]\n\n# Allow cached search only if your AWS GovCloud Region supports web search.\nallowed_web_search_modes = [\"disabled\", \"cached\"]\n\n# Remote control: https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/cli/reference#codex-remote-control\nallow_remote_control = false\n\n# Managed hooks: https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/enterprise/managed-configuration#enforce-managed-hooks-from-requirements\nallow_managed_hooks_only = true\n\ncheck_for_update_on_startup = false\n\n# MCP servers, apps, and plugins are disabled by default.\n# Admins can enable supported integrations after accepting the risks\n# for their use case and configuring access and network controls.\n# https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/enterprise/managed-configuration\nmcp_servers = {}\n\n[features]\napps = false\nplugins = false\n\n# Enable the network proxy for sandboxed commands.\n# https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/agent-approvals-security#network-isolation\nnetwork_proxy = true\n\nrealtime_conversation = false\nimage_generation = false\n\n# Memories: https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/customization/memories\nmemories = false\nexternal_agent_memory_import = false\n\n# We recommend that users review approval requests themselves.\n# Admins can enable automatic review after accepting the risks for their use case.\n# https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/agent-approvals-security#automatic-approval-reviews\nguardian_approval = false\nguardianv2 = false\n\n# Disable background skill-search experiments.\nskill_search = false\n\n# Hooks: https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/hooks\nhooks = false\n\n# If you enable web search, use cached search through Bedrock Mantle\n# where supported by your AWS GovCloud Region.\nstandalone_web_search = false\n\n# Disable feedback submissions to OpenAI.\n[feedback]\nenabled = false\n\n# Network controls for agent commands:\n# https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/enterprise/managed-configuration#configure-network-access-requirements\n[experimental_network]\nenabled = true\nmanaged_allowed_domains_only = true\n\n# No domains allowed by default. Add destinations approved for your use case.\ndomains = {}\n\n# Add approved Unix socket paths here.\nunix_sockets = {}\n\n# Set to true when using an organization-approved upstream proxy.\nallow_upstream_proxy = false\n\n# Keep the command proxy bound to localhost.\ndangerously_allow_non_loopback_proxy = false\ndangerously_allow_all_unix_sockets = false\n\n# Local/private networking: https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/agent-approvals-security#local-and-private-destinations\nallow_local_binding = false\n\n# Application network controls: https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/config-file/config-reference#requirementstoml\n[application.network]\nenabled = true\n\n# Example: Bedrock Mantle in us-gov-west-1.\n# Replace this hostname with the Bedrock endpoint configured in config.toml.\n[application.network.domains]\n\"bedrock-mantle.us-gov-west-1.api.aws\" = \"allow\"\n\n# OpenAI and ChatGPT endpoints.\n# We recommend denying these endpoints to avoid any risk that user data is sent to commercial OpenAI infrastructure.\n\"api.openai.com\" = \"deny\"\n\"chat.openai.com\" = \"deny\"\n\"chatgpt.com\" = \"deny\"\n\"ab.chatgpt.com\" = \"deny\"\n\"platform.openai.com\" = \"deny\"\n\"auth.openai.com\" = \"deny\"\n\"gov.api.openai.com\" = \"deny\"\n\"gov.chatgpt.com\" = \"deny\"\n\"sdfedpreastus2.oaiusercontent.com\" = \"deny\"\n\"o33249.ingest.us.sentry.io\" = \"deny\"\n\"persistent.oaistatic.com\" = \"deny\"\n\"oaisidekickupdates.blob.core.windows.net\" = \"deny\"\n\n# Windows only: https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/config-file/config-reference#requirementstoml\n[windows]\nallowed_sandbox_implementations = [\"elevated\"]\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"2-configure-the-cli\"> 2\\. 配置提供方路由与网络控制 </h2> <p>在 Linux 或 macOS 上，将 <code>config.toml</code> 放到 <code>~/.codex/config.toml</code>；在 Windows 上，放到 <code>%USERPROFILE%\\.codex\\config.toml</code>。如果设置了 <code>CODEX_HOME</code>，请改用其中的 <code>config.toml</code>。用户可以在 <code>requirements.toml</code> 设定的范围内更改这些默认值。</p> <h3 id=\"cli-recommended-configtoml\"> 推荐的 <code>config.toml</code> </h3> <p>下方示例使用 <code>us-gov-west-1</code> 中的 Mantle。请将模型 ID 和 AWS profile 替换为你部署中的实际值。若要使用其他受支持的区域或端点，请同步更新 URL、区域和网络策略。</p> <p>请勿将 AWS 凭据放入 TOML 文件。AWS profile、凭据和凭据助手脚本应放在 Codex CLI 无权修改的文件夹之外。此提供方使用 AWS 凭据；不需要 ChatGPT 登录或 OpenAI API key。请参阅 <a href=\"#/article/a-fc9fbba758a53038?anchor=authentication-options\">Bedrock 身份验证选项</a>。</p> <p>config.toml</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\"># Replace with your approved Bedrock model ID.\nmodel = \"openai.gpt-5.6-terra\"\nmodel_provider = \"amazon-bedrock\"\napproval_policy = { granular = { sandbox_approval = false, rules = true, mcp_elicitations = false, request_permissions = false, skill_approval = true } }\nsandbox_mode = \"workspace-write\"\n\n# Set to \"cached\" only when supported by your model and GovCloud Region\n# and approved for your deployment.\n# https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/web-search.html\nweb_search = \"disabled\"\n\n# Example: Bedrock Mantle in us-gov-west-1.\n[model_providers.amazon-bedrock]\nbase_url = \"https://bedrock-mantle.us-gov-west-1.api.aws/openai/v1\"\nwire_api = \"responses\"\nrequires_openai_auth = false\n\n[model_providers.amazon-bedrock.aws]\nregion = \"us-gov-west-1\"\n\n# Replace with your AWS profile name.\nprofile = \"codex-govcloud\"\n\n[sandbox_workspace_write]\n# Command destinations are controlled by requirements.toml.\nnetwork_access = true\n\n# Disable sending Codex usage analytics to OpenAI.\n[analytics]\nenabled = false\n\n# OpenTelemetry exports are off by default.\n# Admins can configure an approved collector for logs, traces, and metrics.\n# https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/config-file/config-advanced#observability-and-telemetry\n[otel]\nexporter = \"none\"\ntrace_exporter = \"none\"\nmetrics_exporter = \"none\"\nlog_user_prompt = false\n</code></pre> <h3 id=\"cli-apply-network-controls\">应用网络控制</h3> <p>将 Bedrock 等获批的 CLI 端点添加到 <code>application.network.domains</code>。将获批的命令端点添加到 <code>experimental_network.domains</code>。这是两项独立控制：允许模型请求访问 Bedrock，并不代表代理命令也可以连接该服务。</p> <p>在 CLI 0.162.0 中，交互式会话和 <code>codex exec</code> 会将 <code>application.network</code> 应用于 Codex 的模型和服务请求。它不涵盖独立的 <code>codex login</code> 或守护进程更新下载。Codex 的网络设置不能替代设备防火墙。请使用防火墙限制这些目标及凭据助手的网络流量。</p> <h2 id=\"3-verify-the-cli-deployment\">3. 验证部署</h2> <p>更改配置后，请启动新的 CLI 进程。在某个代码库中运行：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-shell\">codex\n</code></pre> <ol> <li>打开 <code>/status</code>，确认模型和提供方，并检查已配置的 AWS profile 是否使用了预期凭据。</li> <li>使用示例数据运行获批的工作流程。</li> <li>确认用户设置和 CLI 标志无法覆盖受管限制。</li> <li>测试无效或过期凭据以及路由失败的情况，并确认内容不会被发送到未获批准的目标。</li> </ol> <p>还应在代码库中检查非交互式使用：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-shell\">codex exec --sandbox read-only \"Reply with exactly: bedrock-ok\"\n</code></pre> <p><code>codex exec</code> 不会提示你批准操作；需要审批的操作会失败。</p> <p>预期输出为 <code>bedrock-ok</code>。请在 CLI 输出中确认提供方和模型；仅凭回复内容本身无法判断请求经过了哪条路由。然后使用获批的工作流程读取一个示例文件，并对 <code>codex exec</code> 重复执行策略检查。</p> <h2 id=\"cli-troubleshooting\">排查常见问题</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>问题</th> <th>检查事项</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>端点不受支持</td> <td>向 OpenAI 确认已安装的 CLI 版本支持该端点和模型。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>AWS 账户或角色不正确</td> <td>检查 <code>model_providers.amazon-bedrock.aws</code> 中的 profile 及其当前凭据。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>限制未生效</td> <td>确认运行 CLI 的计算机已安装 <code>requirements.toml</code>，然后启动新的进程。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>命令无法访问网络</td> <td>检查当前 sandbox、<code>sandbox_workspace_write.network_access</code> 和受管命令域允许列表。默认示例不允许任何命令目的地。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>功能仍不可用</td> <td>查看功能文档，确认所需设置及 Bedrock 支持情况，然后检查网络控制。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"cli-feature-settings\">功能设置</h2> <p>用户无法覆盖由 <code>requirements.toml</code> 强制执行的功能设置。</p> <p>下表总结了上述配置。<strong>On（开启）</strong>表示在受支持的情况下允许使用；其他权限和网络控制仍然适用。</p> <p>有关提供方支持情况，请参阅 <a href=\"#/article/a-fc9fbba758a53038?anchor=feature-availability\">Bedrock 功能可用性</a>。</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>功能</th> <th>默认状态</th> <th>说明</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>本地编码、文件、Git 和子代理</td> <td>On</td> <td>—</td> </tr> <tr> <td>CLI 语音</td> <td>Off</td> <td>—</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-7ea5a1f5cc6a25bc\">记忆</a></td> <td>Off</td> <td>—</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-6e5b50840145f8df\">图像生成</a></td> <td>Off</td> <td>不会阻止输入图像或读取现有图像文件。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-eb946260804133fb\">网页搜索</a></td> <td>Off</td> <td>缓存搜索需要模型和 GovCloud 区域支持。命令网络规则不会限制托管式搜索。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">应用和插件</a></td> <td>Off</td> <td>—</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-77481efb12a63f4e\">已配置的 MCP 服务器</a></td> <td>Off</td> <td>管理员可以在接受相应使用风险并配置访问和网络控制后，启用获批服务器。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-b7af4e0dbfe643b3?anchor=automatic-approval-reviews\">自动审批审查</a></td> <td>Off</td> <td>—</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=codex-remote-control\">远程控制</a></td> <td>Off</td> <td>—</td> </tr> </tbody> </table>","en":"<h1 id=\"bedrock-govcloud-configuration\">Bedrock GovCloud configuration</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>This guide explains how to configure Codex to perform inference against Amazon Bedrock in GovCloud. We cover AWS access, managed device settings, and network controls.</p> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-c2332644faa13713\">Codex configuration reference</a></p> <p>This guide is not legal advice and does not grant an authorization to operate (ATO). Review the configuration, selected AWS services, endpoint controls, and data flows with your security and authorizing officials against your agency’s requirements and system security plan.</p> <h2 id=\"shared-responsibility\">Shared responsibility</h2> <p>Review the <a href=\"https://aws.amazon.com/compliance/shared-responsibility-model/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">AWS shared responsibility model (online)</a> and your selected services’ documentation to understand which controls AWS provides. Your agency is responsible for authorizing their use.</p> <p>In a supported deployment, Codex sends inference requests to the configured Bedrock endpoint using AWS authentication. Your organization secures the devices running Codex, including credentials, repositories, local records, and enabled third-party services. Using GovCloud for inference does not establish that the entire workflow meets your agency’s requirements.</p> <p><strong>govcloud-setup</strong></p> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-f780ae4c53905f80?anchor=3-verify-the-deployment\">Verification checklist</a> · <a href=\"#/article/a-f780ae4c53905f80?anchor=feature-settings\">Feature settings</a></p> <h2 id=\"before-you-begin\">Before you begin</h2> <p>Use desktop app version <strong>26.1002.51308 or later</strong>, as shown in <strong>About</strong>.</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Prepare</th> <th>What you need</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>AWS access</td> <td>An AWS GovCloud account with access to the Bedrock model you’ll use.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Configuration</td> <td>A reviewed <code>requirements.toml</code>, approved network destinations, and rollback instructions.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Device management</td> <td>System configuration or MDM access, with app, device, and agent-command network policies.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"1-deploy-device-requirements\">1. Deploy device requirements</h2> <p>Deploy <code>requirements.toml</code> through system configuration or MDM before app launch. Follow <a href=\"#/article/a-77481efb12a63f4e\">Managed configuration</a> for file locations and MDM delivery. Protect the managed policy and verify its settings on the machine running Codex in <a href=\"#/article/a-f780ae4c53905f80?anchor=3-verify-the-deployment\">step 3</a>.</p> <h3 id=\"recommended-requirementstoml\">Recommended <code>requirements.toml</code></h3> <p>The default <code>requirements.toml</code> below is intentionally restrictive. Administrators can enable additional features if they accept the risk that they pose. Reference the <a href=\"#/article/a-f780ae4c53905f80?anchor=feature-settings\">feature docs</a> and <a href=\"#/article/a-77481efb12a63f4e?anchor=configure-network-access-requirements\">network control docs</a>.</p> <p>requirements.toml</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\"># Disable ChatGPT sign-in.\nallowed_login_methods = [\"api\"]\n\n# https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/agent-approvals-security#common-sandbox-and-approval-combinations\nallowed_sandbox_modes = [\"read-only\", \"workspace-write\"]\n\n# Approval prompts are reviewed by the user.\nallowed_approvals_reviewers = [\"user\"]\nallowed_approval_policies = [\n  { granular = { sandbox_approval = false, rules = true, mcp_elicitations = false, request_permissions = false, skill_approval = true } },\n]\n\n# Allow cached search only if your AWS GovCloud Region supports web search.\nallowed_web_search_modes = [\"disabled\", \"cached\"]\n\n# Block agent browser use and native-app control.\nallow_browser_and_computer_use = false\n\n# Appshots: https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/appshots\nallow_appshots = false\n\n# Remote control: https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/remote-connections#pick-up-work-from-another-device\nallow_remote_control = false\n\n# Managed hooks: https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/enterprise/managed-configuration#enforce-managed-hooks-from-requirements\nallow_managed_hooks_only = true\n\ncheck_for_update_on_startup = false\n\n# MCP servers, apps, and plugins are disabled by default.\n# Admins can enable supported integrations after accepting the risks\n# for their use case and configuring access and network controls.\n# https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/enterprise/managed-configuration\nmcp_servers = {}\n\n[features]\napps = false\nenable_mcp_apps = false\nplugins = false\n\n# Enable the network proxy for sandboxed commands.\n# https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/agent-approvals-security#network-isolation\nnetwork_proxy = true\n\nin_app_dictation = false\nrealtime_conversation = false\n\n# Browser controls: https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/enterprise/managed-configuration#disable-codex-feature-surfaces\n# Note that both browser use and computer use are up to your organization's risk appetite.\n# An agent using your browser or computer may navigate to any websites or applications that the\n# computer has access to. OpenAI does not currently provide additional protections restricting\n# the network paths that browser use and computer use may exercise.\nin_app_browser = false\nbrowser_use = false\nbrowser_use_external = false\nbrowser_use_full_cdp_access = false\n\n# Computer Use: https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/computer-use\n# Enable after accepting the risks and configuring app and network access.\ncomputer_use = false\n\n# Set to true to let users update through the app.\n# App-store, package-manager, and MDM updates are controlled separately.\n# https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/enterprise/manage-app-updates#turn-off-in-app-updates\nin_app_updates = false\n\nimage_generation = false\n\n# Memories: https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/customization/memories\nmemories = false\n\n# Computer History: https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/customization/computer-history\nchronicle = false\n\nexternal_agent_memory_import = false\n\n# We recommend that users review approval requests themselves.\n# Admins can enable automatic review after accepting the risks for their use case.\n# https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/agent-approvals-security#automatic-approval-reviews\nguardian_approval = false\nguardianv2 = false\n\n# Disable background skill-search experiments.\nskill_search = false\n\n# Hooks: https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/hooks\nhooks = false\n\n# If you enable web search, use cached search through Bedrock Mantle\n# where supported by your AWS GovCloud Region.\nstandalone_web_search = false\n\n# Disable feedback submissions to OpenAI.\n[feedback]\nenabled = false\n\n# Network controls for agent commands:\n# https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/enterprise/managed-configuration#configure-network-access-requirements\n[experimental_network]\nenabled = true\nmanaged_allowed_domains_only = true\n\n# No domains allowed by default. Add destinations approved for your use case.\ndomains = {}\n\n# Add approved Unix socket paths here.\nunix_sockets = {}\n\n# Set to true when using an organization-approved upstream proxy.\nallow_upstream_proxy = false\n\n# Keep the command proxy bound to localhost.\ndangerously_allow_non_loopback_proxy = false\ndangerously_allow_all_unix_sockets = false\n\n# Local/private networking: https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/agent-approvals-security#local-and-private-destinations\nallow_local_binding = false\n\n# App network controls: https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/enterprise/managed-configuration#control-desktop-app-network-destinations\n[application.network]\nenabled = true\n\n# Example: Bedrock Mantle in us-gov-west-1.\n# Replace this hostname with the Bedrock endpoint configured in config.toml.\n[application.network.domains]\n\"bedrock-mantle.us-gov-west-1.api.aws\" = \"allow\"\n\n# OpenAI and ChatGPT endpoints.\n# We recommend denying these endpoints to avoid any risk that user data is sent to commercial OpenAI infrastructure.\n\"api.openai.com\" = \"deny\"\n\"chat.openai.com\" = \"deny\"\n\"chatgpt.com\" = \"deny\"\n\"ab.chatgpt.com\" = \"deny\"\n\"platform.openai.com\" = \"deny\"\n\"auth.openai.com\" = \"deny\"\n\"gov.api.openai.com\" = \"deny\"\n\"gov.chatgpt.com\" = \"deny\"\n\"sdfedpreastus2.oaiusercontent.com\" = \"deny\"\n\"o33249.ingest.us.sentry.io\" = \"deny\"\n\"persistent.oaistatic.com\" = \"deny\"\n\"oaisidekickupdates.blob.core.windows.net\" = \"deny\"\n\n# Windows only: https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/config-file/config-reference#requirementstoml\n[windows]\nallowed_sandbox_implementations = [\"elevated\"]\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"2-configure-provider-routing-and-network-controls\">2. Configure provider routing and network controls</h2> <p>Set the provider, model, Region, and endpoint in <code>config.toml</code> or managed defaults. Users can change these defaults within the limits set by <code>requirements.toml</code>.</p> <h3 id=\"recommended-configtoml\">Recommended <code>config.toml</code></h3> <p>The example below uses Mantle in <code>us-gov-west-1</code>. Replace the model ID and AWS profile with your deployment’s values. For another supported Region or endpoint, update the URL, Region, and network policy together.</p> <p>The example turns off optional diagnostics and data sharing. Keep AWS credentials outside the TOML file. Keep the AWS profile, credentials, and credential helper scripts outside folders Codex can modify.</p> <p>config.toml</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\"># Replace with your approved Bedrock model ID.\nmodel = \"openai.gpt-5.6-terra\"\nmodel_provider = \"amazon-bedrock\"\napproval_policy = { granular = { sandbox_approval = false, rules = true, mcp_elicitations = false, request_permissions = false, skill_approval = true } }\nsandbox_mode = \"workspace-write\"\n\n# Set to \"cached\" only when supported by your model and GovCloud Region\n# and approved for your deployment.\n# https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/web-search.html\nweb_search = \"disabled\"\n\n# Example: Bedrock Mantle in us-gov-west-1.\n[model_providers.amazon-bedrock]\nbase_url = \"https://bedrock-mantle.us-gov-west-1.api.aws/openai/v1\"\nwire_api = \"responses\"\nrequires_openai_auth = false\n\n[model_providers.amazon-bedrock.aws]\nregion = \"us-gov-west-1\"\n\n# Replace with your AWS profile name.\nprofile = \"codex-govcloud\"\n\n[sandbox_workspace_write]\n# Command destinations are controlled by requirements.toml.\nnetwork_access = true\n\n# Disable sending Codex usage analytics to OpenAI.\n[analytics]\nenabled = false\n\n# OpenTelemetry exports are off by default.\n# Admins can configure an approved collector for logs, traces, and metrics.\n# https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/config-file/config-advanced#observability-and-telemetry\n[otel]\nexporter = \"none\"\ntrace_exporter = \"none\"\nmetrics_exporter = \"none\"\nlog_user_prompt = false\n</code></pre> <p>This example uses AWS credentials with Bedrock Mantle. For Bedrock Runtime or a gateway, follow the <a href=\"#/article/a-fc9fbba758a53038\">provider setup instructions</a>.</p> <h3 id=\"apply-network-controls\">Apply network controls</h3> <p>Add approved app destinations, including Bedrock, to <a href=\"#/article/a-77481efb12a63f4e?anchor=control-desktop-app-network-destinations\"><code>application.network.domains</code></a>. Add approved command destinations to <a href=\"#/article/a-77481efb12a63f4e?anchor=configure-network-access-requirements\"><code>experimental_network.domains</code></a>.</p> <p>Codex’s network settings do not replace your device firewall.</p> <h2 id=\"3-verify-the-deployment\">3. Verify the deployment</h2> <ol> <li>Confirm that your policy is active and Codex is using the intended AWS credentials and Bedrock settings.</li> <li>Run an approved workflow with sample data.</li> <li>Confirm that user settings cannot override the managed restrictions.</li> <li>Test invalid or expired credentials and routing failures. Confirm that content is not sent to an unapproved destination.</li> </ol> <h2 id=\"troubleshoot-common-problems\">Troubleshoot common problems</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Problem</th> <th>What to check</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Unsupported endpoint</td> <td>Confirm with OpenAI that your installed desktop and app-server versions support the endpoint and model.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Wrong AWS account or role</td> <td>Check the active credentials and selected AWS profile. A Bedrock API key may take precedence over the profile.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Restrictions aren’t applied</td> <td>Confirm the intended <code>requirements.toml</code> is loaded on the machine running Codex.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Feature still unavailable</td> <td>Check the feature docs for required settings and Bedrock support, then check your network controls.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"feature-settings\">Feature settings</h2> <p>Users cannot override feature settings enforced by <code>requirements.toml</code>.</p> <p>The table summarizes the configuration above. <strong>On</strong> means permitted where supported; other permissions and network controls still apply.</p> <p>For provider support, see <a href=\"#/article/a-fc9fbba758a53038?anchor=feature-availability\">Bedrock feature availability</a>.</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Feature</th> <th>Default</th> <th>Notes</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Local coding, files, Git, and subagents</td> <td>On</td> <td>—</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-b5406e60cbfa0b68\">Local scheduled tasks</a></td> <td>On</td> <td>—</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-a7de5b39bd26a809\">Browser</a></td> <td>Off</td> <td>Includes the built-in browser, connected browsers, agent browser control, and Developer mode.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-7be3f970bd43699c\">Computer Use</a> and <a href=\"#/article/a-c302b8efa03eab38\">Appshots</a></td> <td>Off</td> <td>—</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-7ea5a1f5cc6a25bc\">Memory</a> and <a href=\"#/article/a-f3a0216fc3d2956b\">Computer History</a></td> <td>Off</td> <td>—</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-6e5b50840145f8df\">Image generation</a></td> <td>Off</td> <td>Does not block image inputs or reading existing image files.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-eb946260804133fb\">Web search</a></td> <td>Off</td> <td>Cached search requires support in your model and GovCloud Region. Command-network rules do not restrict hosted search.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">Apps and plugins</a></td> <td>Off</td> <td>—</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-77481efb12a63f4e\">Configured MCP servers</a></td> <td>Off</td> <td>Admins can enable approved servers after accepting the risks for their use case and configuring access and network controls.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Interactive MCP apps</td> <td>Off</td> <td>—</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Dictation</td> <td>Off</td> <td>—</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-b7af4e0dbfe643b3?anchor=automatic-approval-reviews\">Automatic approval review</a></td> <td>Off</td> <td>—</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-171fdaa74f75310f?anchor=pick-up-work-from-another-device\">Remote control</a></td> <td>Off</td> <td>SSH connections are separate.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-24c62848a3326493\">App updates</a></td> <td>Off</td> <td>—</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>Enabling agent browser use or Computer Use also requires <code>allow_browser_and_computer_use = true</code>.</p> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-f780ae4c53905f80?anchor=3-verify-the-cli-deployment\">Verification checklist</a> · <a href=\"#/article/a-f780ae4c53905f80?anchor=cli-feature-settings\">Feature settings</a></p> <p>Configure Codex CLI to perform inference against Amazon Bedrock in GovCloud. The <a href=\"#/article/a-f780ae4c53905f80?anchor=shared-responsibility\">shared responsibility guidance</a> also applies to CLI deployments.</p> <h2 id=\"cli-prerequisites\">Before you begin</h2> <p>Install <a href=\"#/article/a-24d888be8e5fa72d\">Codex CLI</a> and check the installed version:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-shell\">codex --version\n</code></pre> <p>Use <strong>Codex CLI 0.162.0 or newer</strong>.</p> <p>You need an AWS GovCloud account with access to the Bedrock model you’ll use, and administrator access to deploy <code>requirements.toml</code> on the machine running Codex. For WSL or SSH, apply the configuration inside the environment where the CLI runs.</p> <h2 id=\"1-deploy-cli-requirements\">1. Deploy device requirements</h2> <p>Deploy <code>requirements.toml</code> through system configuration or MDM before CLI launch. Follow <a href=\"#/article/a-77481efb12a63f4e\">Managed configuration</a> for file locations and MDM delivery. Protect the managed policy and verify its settings on the machine running Codex in <a href=\"#/article/a-f780ae4c53905f80?anchor=3-verify-the-cli-deployment\">step 3</a>.</p> <h3 id=\"cli-recommended-requirementstoml\"> Recommended <code>requirements.toml</code> </h3> <p>The default <code>requirements.toml</code> below is intentionally restrictive. Administrators can enable additional features if they accept the risk that they pose. Reference the <a href=\"#/article/a-f780ae4c53905f80?anchor=cli-feature-settings\">feature docs</a> and <a href=\"#/article/a-77481efb12a63f4e?anchor=configure-network-access-requirements\">network control docs</a>.</p> <p>requirements.toml</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\"># Disable ChatGPT sign-in.\nallowed_login_methods = [\"api\"]\n\n# https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/agent-approvals-security#common-sandbox-and-approval-combinations\nallowed_sandbox_modes = [\"read-only\", \"workspace-write\"]\n\n# Approval prompts are reviewed by the user.\nallowed_approvals_reviewers = [\"user\"]\nallowed_approval_policies = [\n  { granular = { sandbox_approval = false, rules = true, mcp_elicitations = false, request_permissions = false, skill_approval = true } },\n]\n\n# Allow cached search only if your AWS GovCloud Region supports web search.\nallowed_web_search_modes = [\"disabled\", \"cached\"]\n\n# Remote control: https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/cli/reference#codex-remote-control\nallow_remote_control = false\n\n# Managed hooks: https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/enterprise/managed-configuration#enforce-managed-hooks-from-requirements\nallow_managed_hooks_only = true\n\ncheck_for_update_on_startup = false\n\n# MCP servers, apps, and plugins are disabled by default.\n# Admins can enable supported integrations after accepting the risks\n# for their use case and configuring access and network controls.\n# https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/enterprise/managed-configuration\nmcp_servers = {}\n\n[features]\napps = false\nplugins = false\n\n# Enable the network proxy for sandboxed commands.\n# https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/agent-approvals-security#network-isolation\nnetwork_proxy = true\n\nrealtime_conversation = false\nimage_generation = false\n\n# Memories: https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/customization/memories\nmemories = false\nexternal_agent_memory_import = false\n\n# We recommend that users review approval requests themselves.\n# Admins can enable automatic review after accepting the risks for their use case.\n# https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/agent-approvals-security#automatic-approval-reviews\nguardian_approval = false\nguardianv2 = false\n\n# Disable background skill-search experiments.\nskill_search = false\n\n# Hooks: https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/hooks\nhooks = false\n\n# If you enable web search, use cached search through Bedrock Mantle\n# where supported by your AWS GovCloud Region.\nstandalone_web_search = false\n\n# Disable feedback submissions to OpenAI.\n[feedback]\nenabled = false\n\n# Network controls for agent commands:\n# https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/enterprise/managed-configuration#configure-network-access-requirements\n[experimental_network]\nenabled = true\nmanaged_allowed_domains_only = true\n\n# No domains allowed by default. Add destinations approved for your use case.\ndomains = {}\n\n# Add approved Unix socket paths here.\nunix_sockets = {}\n\n# Set to true when using an organization-approved upstream proxy.\nallow_upstream_proxy = false\n\n# Keep the command proxy bound to localhost.\ndangerously_allow_non_loopback_proxy = false\ndangerously_allow_all_unix_sockets = false\n\n# Local/private networking: https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/agent-approvals-security#local-and-private-destinations\nallow_local_binding = false\n\n# Application network controls: https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/config-file/config-reference#requirementstoml\n[application.network]\nenabled = true\n\n# Example: Bedrock Mantle in us-gov-west-1.\n# Replace this hostname with the Bedrock endpoint configured in config.toml.\n[application.network.domains]\n\"bedrock-mantle.us-gov-west-1.api.aws\" = \"allow\"\n\n# OpenAI and ChatGPT endpoints.\n# We recommend denying these endpoints to avoid any risk that user data is sent to commercial OpenAI infrastructure.\n\"api.openai.com\" = \"deny\"\n\"chat.openai.com\" = \"deny\"\n\"chatgpt.com\" = \"deny\"\n\"ab.chatgpt.com\" = \"deny\"\n\"platform.openai.com\" = \"deny\"\n\"auth.openai.com\" = \"deny\"\n\"gov.api.openai.com\" = \"deny\"\n\"gov.chatgpt.com\" = \"deny\"\n\"sdfedpreastus2.oaiusercontent.com\" = \"deny\"\n\"o33249.ingest.us.sentry.io\" = \"deny\"\n\"persistent.oaistatic.com\" = \"deny\"\n\"oaisidekickupdates.blob.core.windows.net\" = \"deny\"\n\n# Windows only: https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/config-file/config-reference#requirementstoml\n[windows]\nallowed_sandbox_implementations = [\"elevated\"]\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"2-configure-the-cli\"> 2\\. Configure provider routing and network controls </h2> <p>Put <code>config.toml</code> in <code>~/.codex/config.toml</code> on Linux or macOS, or <code>%USERPROFILE%\\.codex\\config.toml</code> on Windows. If you set <code>CODEX_HOME</code>, use its <code>config.toml</code> instead. Users can change these defaults within the limits set by <code>requirements.toml</code>.</p> <h3 id=\"cli-recommended-configtoml\"> Recommended <code>config.toml</code> </h3> <p>The example uses Mantle in <code>us-gov-west-1</code>. Replace the model ID and AWS profile with your deployment’s values. For another supported Region or endpoint, update the URL, Region, and network policy together.</p> <p>Keep AWS credentials outside the TOML file. Keep the AWS profile, credentials, and credential helper scripts outside folders Codex can modify. The CLI uses AWS credentials for this provider; ChatGPT sign-in and an OpenAI API key are not required. See <a href=\"#/article/a-fc9fbba758a53038?anchor=authentication-options\">Bedrock authentication options</a>.</p> <p>config.toml</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\"># Replace with your approved Bedrock model ID.\nmodel = \"openai.gpt-5.6-terra\"\nmodel_provider = \"amazon-bedrock\"\napproval_policy = { granular = { sandbox_approval = false, rules = true, mcp_elicitations = false, request_permissions = false, skill_approval = true } }\nsandbox_mode = \"workspace-write\"\n\n# Set to \"cached\" only when supported by your model and GovCloud Region\n# and approved for your deployment.\n# https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/web-search.html\nweb_search = \"disabled\"\n\n# Example: Bedrock Mantle in us-gov-west-1.\n[model_providers.amazon-bedrock]\nbase_url = \"https://bedrock-mantle.us-gov-west-1.api.aws/openai/v1\"\nwire_api = \"responses\"\nrequires_openai_auth = false\n\n[model_providers.amazon-bedrock.aws]\nregion = \"us-gov-west-1\"\n\n# Replace with your AWS profile name.\nprofile = \"codex-govcloud\"\n\n[sandbox_workspace_write]\n# Command destinations are controlled by requirements.toml.\nnetwork_access = true\n\n# Disable sending Codex usage analytics to OpenAI.\n[analytics]\nenabled = false\n\n# OpenTelemetry exports are off by default.\n# Admins can configure an approved collector for logs, traces, and metrics.\n# https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/config-file/config-advanced#observability-and-telemetry\n[otel]\nexporter = \"none\"\ntrace_exporter = \"none\"\nmetrics_exporter = \"none\"\nlog_user_prompt = false\n</code></pre> <h3 id=\"cli-apply-network-controls\">Apply network controls</h3> <p>Add approved CLI destinations, including Bedrock, to <code>application.network.domains</code>. Add approved command destinations to <code>experimental_network.domains</code>. These are separate controls: allowing Bedrock for model requests does not allow agent commands to contact it.</p> <p>In CLI 0.162.0, interactive sessions and <code>codex exec</code> apply <code>application.network</code> to Codex’s model and service requests. It does not cover standalone <code>codex login</code> or daemon update downloads. Codex’s network settings do not replace your device firewall. Use the firewall to restrict those destinations and credential-helper traffic.</p> <h2 id=\"3-verify-the-cli-deployment\">3. Verify the deployment</h2> <p>Start a new CLI process after changing the configuration. From a repository, run:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-shell\">codex\n</code></pre> <ol> <li>Open <code>/status</code> and confirm the model and provider. Check that the configured AWS profile uses the intended credentials.</li> <li>Run an approved workflow with sample data.</li> <li>Confirm that user settings and CLI flags cannot override the managed restrictions.</li> <li>Test invalid or expired credentials and routing failures. Confirm that content is not sent to an unapproved destination.</li> </ol> <p>Also check non-interactive use from a repository:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-shell\">codex exec --sandbox read-only \"Reply with exactly: bedrock-ok\"\n</code></pre> <p><code>codex exec</code> does not prompt for approval; actions that require approval fail.</p> <p>Expect <code>bedrock-ok</code>. Confirm the provider and model in the CLI output; the reply alone does not identify the route. Follow with an approved workflow that reads a sample file, and repeat the policy checks for <code>codex exec</code>.</p> <h2 id=\"cli-troubleshooting\">Troubleshoot common problems</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Problem</th> <th>What to check</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Unsupported endpoint</td> <td>Confirm with OpenAI that your installed CLI version supports the endpoint and model.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Wrong AWS account or role</td> <td>Check the profile in <code>model_providers.amazon-bedrock.aws</code> and its active credentials.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Restrictions aren’t applied</td> <td>Confirm <code>requirements.toml</code> is installed on the machine running the CLI, then start a new process.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>A command cannot access the network</td> <td>Check the active sandbox, <code>sandbox_workspace_write.network_access</code>, and the managed command-domain allowlist. The sample allows no command destinations by default.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Feature still unavailable</td> <td>Check the feature docs for required settings and Bedrock support, then check your network controls.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"cli-feature-settings\">Feature settings</h2> <p>Users cannot override feature settings enforced by <code>requirements.toml</code>.</p> <p>The table summarizes the configuration above. <strong>On</strong> means permitted where supported; other permissions and network controls still apply.</p> <p>For provider support, see <a href=\"#/article/a-fc9fbba758a53038?anchor=feature-availability\">Bedrock feature availability</a>.</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Feature</th> <th>Default</th> <th>Notes</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Local coding, files, Git, and subagents</td> <td>On</td> <td>—</td> </tr> <tr> <td>CLI voice</td> <td>Off</td> <td>—</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-7ea5a1f5cc6a25bc\">Memory</a></td> <td>Off</td> <td>—</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-6e5b50840145f8df\">Image generation</a></td> <td>Off</td> <td>Does not block image inputs or reading existing image files.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-eb946260804133fb\">Web search</a></td> <td>Off</td> <td>Cached search requires support in your model and GovCloud Region. Command-network rules do not restrict hosted search.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">Apps and plugins</a></td> <td>Off</td> <td>—</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-77481efb12a63f4e\">Configured MCP servers</a></td> <td>Off</td> <td>Admins can enable approved servers after accepting the risks for their use case and configuring access and network controls.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-b7af4e0dbfe643b3?anchor=automatic-approval-reviews\">Automatic approval review</a></td> <td>Off</td> <td>—</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=codex-remote-control\">Remote control</a></td> <td>Off</td> <td>—</td> </tr> </tbody> </table>"};
